<title>MOROCCO: Morocco mulls partly privatising state airline.</title>
<headline>Morocco mulls partly privatising state airline.</headline>
<dateline>RABAT 1997-06-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Morocco is looking at a plan to open up part of the capital of the state-owned airline, Royal Air Maroc, to private investors to help upgrade the flag carrier, the official news agency MAP said on Sunday.</p>
<p>MAP quoted Transport Minister Said Ameskane as saying at the weekend that the airline's some 27-strong fleet of planes was well short of the capability to compete in an increasingly liberalised world of air transport.</p>
<p>Royal Air Maroc made a profit of about 140 million dirhams ($14.8 million) profit in 1996, according to MAP.</p>
</text>
